                <pb facs="0284" n="178" sameAs="frus:frus1891/pg178"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Egan</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic">October 1,
                        1891</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. Egan is instructed to inform the Department, by cable, of the essential parts
                    of notes from the foreign office, and to keep it fully advised as to the facts
                    respecting his legation and those of other Governments. He is to report fully by
                    mail (sending copies of all correspondence) all instances of disrespect to the
                    legations and all incidents of arrests of Americans.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
